summary: 1479560-syscall-nmi-stackp-race regression test
description: |+
    Stack pointer got corrupted while syscall entry path
    race with nmi patch, which can lead to kernel panic
    as result of running in user stack.

    smep supported (cpu flag) machine can reproduce this easily,
    have not reproduced this with non smep systems.

    #1479560 Timing/race between system_call() and nmi_handle()->
    arch_trigger_all_cpu_backtrace_handler() causes page fault -
    protection violation on user mode stack address.

contact: Chunyu Hu <chuhu@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - gcc
  - glibc
recommend: []
duration: 10m
extra-summary: /kernel/general/scheduler/1479560-syscall-nmi-stackp-race
extra-task: /kernel/general/scheduler/1479560-syscall-nmi-stackp-race
